g popularity alongside hip hop and EDM during the 2010s. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"MTV Europe Music Award for Best New Act (2004)","body":"Won.","year":2004,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q38430"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best New Artist (2005)","body":"Nominated.","year":2005,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1453643"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"NRJ Music Award for International Revelation of the Year (2005)","body":"Won.","year":2005,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3334531"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"NRJ Music Award for International Song of the Year (2005) — This Love","body":"Won.","year":2005,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3334529"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Pop Vocal Album (2012) — Overexposed","body":"Nominated.","year":2012,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1027891"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"NRJ Music Award for International Group/Duo/Troupe of the Year (2015)","body":"Won.","year":2015,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3334537"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"NRJ Music Award for International Song of the Year (2018) — Girls Like You","body":"Won.","year":2018,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3334529"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Sex and Candy (1997) - Major Hit","body":null,"year":1997,"extra":{"from":"Marcy Playground","from_id":256647995921745,"type":"song"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Great Alt-Rock One-Hit Wonders of the 90s: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d_uDHds2XGQ"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Early Gigs (2008-2009)","body":"Fitz and The Tantrums began playing gigs at the end of 2008, continuing through 2009, and by the end of 2009, they were opening shows for Maroon 5. \"Bigs began at the end of 2008 and continued through the next 12 months. A debut EP was recorded in early 2009, and by the end of the year, they were opening shows for Maroon 5.\"","year":2008,"extra":{"from":"Fitz and The Tantrums","from_id":57207342550255,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Late Bloomers","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P45lJTdneoI"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Justin Bieber was a key figure in the rise of pop music that contributed to rock being \"swamped\" around 2011-2012, demonstrating the genre's widespread appeal and strength during the 2010s. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Justin Bieber","from_id":103038387250175,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Rihanna was a significant artist during the period of pop music dominance that overshadowed rock by 2011-2012, as the genre gained increasing strength alongside hip hop and EDM. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Rihanna","from_id":235023506806646,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Katy Perry played a role in the ascendance of pop music that led to rock being \"swamped\" by 2011 or 2012, reflecting the genre's increasing cultural strength throughout the 2010s. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Katy Perry","from_id":209881053853865,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Carly Rae Jepsen was among the pop artists who were part of the genre's significant rise in the 2010s, contributing to a period where pop, hip hop, and EDM collectively overshadowed rock music around 2011-2012. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Carly Rae Jepsen","from_id":235175259843757,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Pop Dominance in 2010s","body":"Adele was a major pop artist whose popularity contributed to the overall rise of pop music that \"swamped\" rock by 2011 or 2012, signifying the genre's significant cultural influence during the decade. \"And you can make the argument that it certainly did swamp by not only a rise in pop music, you know, Maroon 5, Justin Bieber, Rihanna, Pink Kitty Perry, Carly Recepcion, Adele, but also by the increasing strength of hip hop and the big beats and bass lines of EDM.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Adele","from_id":74050265053328,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 1: Rock Struggles Again","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5Y6nHw5xx88"}]}],"charts":[{"id":276240810531719,"type":"album","name":"Songs About Jane","list_id":200600589539543,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Funk Rock","src":"musthear","rank":179,"year":2002,"note":null,"yt":"nsobZOfLYlg","scaruffi":null},{"id":103564494700656,"type":"song","name":"This Love","work_year":2004,"list_id":205173146701366,"list":"Billboard Year-End 2004","src":"singles","rank":4,"year":2004,"note":"","yt":"XPpTgCho5ZA","scaruffi":null},{"id":87052807417558,"type":"song","name":"She Will Be Loved","work_year":2004,"list_id":205173146701366,"list":"Billboard Year-End 2004","src":"singles","rank":35,"year":2004,"note":"","yt":"nIjVuRTm-dc","scaruffi":null},{"id":103564494700656,"type":"song","name":"This Love","work_year":2004,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":4,"year":2004,"note":null,"yt":"XPpTgCho5ZA","scaruffi":null},{"id":87052807417558,"type":"song","name":"She Will Be Loved","work_year":2004,"list_id":258416889310056,"list":"Billboard Year-End 2005","src":"singles","rank":61,"yea